Make subprocess work on a fork-less platform (wasm) via os.posix_spawn().

wasm32-unknown-linux-musl has no working fork(): musl exposes the symbol but
the clone/fork syscall fails at runtime, so _posixsubprocess (fork_exec) is not
built (py_cv_module__posixsubprocess=n/a). Upstream subprocess falls back to
fork_exec for anything the posix_spawn() fast path does not cover (bare program
names resolved via PATH, close_fds without addclosefrom_np, ...), which cannot
work here. Route every child launch through os.posix_spawn() when fork_exec is
unavailable: tolerate a missing _posixsubprocess at import, force
_USE_POSIX_SPAWN on, only emit POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSEFROM where the platform has it
(musl lacks addclosefrom_np, so os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSEFROM is absent), and in the
POSIX _execute_child resolve a bare program name against PATH before spawning.
preexec_fn/pass_fds cannot be honoured without fork(), so they raise
NotImplementedError rather than being silently ignored.

--- a/Lib/subprocess.py
+++ b/Lib/subprocess.py
